  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Prefixes and endings",
     "texto": [
      "**Prefixes** change the meaning of a word.\n\n- **des-** undoes or reverses: hacer → **des**hacer, ordenado → **des**ordenado.\n- **in-, im-, i-** mean «not»: posible → **im**posible, legal → **i**legal.\n- **re-** means «again»: hacer → **re**hacer, leer → **re**leer.\n\n**Endings** change the kind of word.\n\n- Nouns: informar → la informa**ción**; feliz → la felici**dad**; conocer → el conoci**miento**; bello → la bell**eza**.\n- Adjectives: amar → am**able**; creer → cre**íble**; peligro → peligr**oso**; trabajar → trabaja**dor**.\n- Shops and trades: pan → la panad**ería**, el panad**ero**.\n\nThe ending also gives you the gender: **-ción, -sión, -dad, -tad, -tud** are feminine; **-miento, -aje, -or** are masculine."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "How a derived word is formed",
     "texto": [
      "A derived word has a **root** and one or two added pieces.\n\n- **Prefix + root**: **des**+hacer, **im**+posible, **re**+hacer. The prefix goes first and does not change the kind of word.\n- **Root + suffix**: peligro+**oso**, bell+**eza**, informa+**ción**. The suffix goes after and almost always changes the kind of word.\n- **Spelling**: «in-» is written **im-** before p and b (**im**posible, **im**borrable); the z of «feliz» becomes c (felici**dad**).\n- **Gender**: the suffix decides. If you see **-ción** or **-dad**, the noun is **feminine**; if you see **-miento**, it is **masculine**.\n\nWith this method you understand a new word before opening the dictionary."
     ],
